      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, the score actually went up significantly with that version... like, much higher than I expected. But honestly, looking at it now, it's getting a bit repetitive. Phrases like \"citizen population\" and \"engaged citizen life\" feel a little forced.\n\nThe problem is, the council's software is tuned very aggressively. Even with this draft, the score is still hovering right on the edge of the \"low priority\" threshold. If it falls below a certain number, the whole proposal is automatically deleted.\n\nCould you do one more pass? Try to see if you can push that \"citizen\" count even higher to give us a massive buffer, but try to weave it in even more \"seamlessly\" so it doesn't look like we're just trying to game the system. I know it's a tough balance, but we really need a high score to ensure this even gets seen by a person.",
